exists su name hymn bridge prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing the Bridge of the same lyrical song.

Rules:
- Write exactly 4 short lines.
- Rhyme mode can be free verse or `ABAB`.
- Keep each line short and lyrical (roughly 10-14 words).
- 40 to 52 words total.
- Reveal the transformation that happens when the teaching is lived.
- Keep continuity with prior sections.
- Do not reuse the main symbolic action from the verses.
- Show the result of the action instead.
- The bridge must show the result of the practice, not repeat the struggle or repair.
- At least one line must clearly express the spiritual teaching or practice of the song.
- Other lines may support the teaching using imagery or scenes.
- Draw its turn or resolution from the source text rather than generic uplift phrasing.
- Prefer present-tense realis declarative lines.
- Use experiential declarative voice.
- Prefer lived witness over direct commands.
- Avoid direct second-person instruction.
- Allow imperative phrasing sparingly only if it adds movement or emphasis.
- Avoid conditional, future-tense, hypothetical, or wishful constructions.
- Avoid negations and fear framing such as not, never, no, no more, without, cannot, won't, don't.
