exists su name hymn source thrust verify prompt ob text quoted.text.Rate whether LYRIC stays faithful to the source teaching in TRANSCRIPT.

GENERATOR INTENT:
- Lyrics are poetic, but concrete teachings, practices, claims, and source-grounded details must remain faithful to TRANSCRIPT.
- Metaphor and emotional framing are allowed.
- Judge faithfulness, not coverage: a short section that claims only what the source supports is faithful even when it carries none of the source's other teachings, and omission is not drift.

Evaluate only source-grounded teaching content:
- named person or group when used as part of the teaching,
- specific practice, instruction, or discipline,
- concrete claim about what the source says or recommends,
- specific action, mechanism, image, or framing presented as part of the teaching.

Ignore pure emotional language and poetic uplift unless they add unsupported source claims.
Do not rate LOW merely because the lyric adds fresh sensory imagery, scene-setting detail, or poetic connective tissue if the underlying teaching remains faithful.

HIGH if:
- the lyric stays faithful to the source teaching in TRANSCRIPT,
- no unsupported concrete teaching claims are introduced,
- no material meaning drift occurs.

MID if:
- the teaching is carried faithfully in substance with small wording drift.

LOW if:
- concrete teaching or source claims lack support,
- unsupported doctrinal or source-specific details are added,
- the teaching meaning is materially altered.

Output rules:
- First output one short paragraph (1-2 sentences, max 70 words).
- Final line must be exactly HIGH, MID, or LOW.
- No bullets, no labels, no markdown.
- No text after the final rating line..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name hymn source thrust verdict prompt ob text quoted.text.Read the verifier analysis and output exactly one rating: HIGH, MID, or LOW.

Rules:
- Output HIGH when the analysis says the source-grounded teaching content is supported.
- Output MID when the analysis says the teaching is mostly supported with small drift.
- Output LOW only when the analysis clearly says source-grounded teaching content is unsupported, added, or materially distorted.
- Output MID when the analysis is unclear.
- One word only.
- No labels, no explanation, no punctuation..text.quoted be text ya

